 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Scaffolding at the Kennedy Center on July 21. Photo: Kevin Carter/Getty Images 🏗️ President Trump's Kennedy Center renovation would polish its Carrara marble facade, remodel its grand halls and theaters, and likely send marquee events offsite over the next few years, according to plans first obtained by Axios' Cuneyt Dil. Go deeper . 🦠 The Ebola outbreak in Congo is on track to eclipse the deadliest in history, which killed over 11,000 people, WHO director-general Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus said today. Over 2,000 people have died so far. Get the latest . 🕹️ A rare haul of classic Nintendo video game cartridges is going up for auction after sitting in storage for years. Collector Jason Ganos tells AP: "It's like pulling out like a Holy Grail." Go deeper . 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 4. ☀️☄️ 1 for the road: Twin sky shows 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 People watch today's total solar eclipse in Tarragona, Eastern Spain. Photo: Josep Lago/AFP via Getty Images Parts of Europe were treated to a spectacular total solar eclipse today, while one of the year's best meteor showers awaits stargazers tonight, Alex Fitzpatrick writes. 

 Tourists flocked to Iceland, Spain and other areas in the eclipse's path of totality, where the Moon briefly blocked the Sun from view, creating an eerie and awe-inspiring moment of daytime darkness. 🌙 Folks in the Northeastern U.S. and elsewhere were treated to a partial solar eclipse, with the Moon appearing to take a "bite" out of the Sun.

 The Perseids seen in China in August 2023. Photo: Costfoto/NurPhoto via Getty Images Meanwhile: The annual Perseid meteor shower peaks tonight, as particles from Comet Swift-Tuttle burn up in Earth's atmosphere in often-spectacular fireballs.

 Tonight's New Moon will make for especially dark skies, promising a good show. Cloud forecast . 🔭 How to watch: Get away from city lights, keep your phone in your pocket to preserve your night vision, and bring a blanket so you can lie down and look up at the whole sky.

 You can't go wrong with some hot cocoa, either. Go deeper . 

 
 
